        "description": "This course is an advanced form of an introductory algorithms course, and is meant to have a thorough grounding in core Algorithms required for pursuing PG degree in Computer Science. The course covers topics such as asymptotic notation, recurrence relation, graph algorithms, heaps, dynamic programming, greedy algorithms, divide and conquer, NP-completeness where the UG contents of each topic is first reviewed in a fast-paced manner, and is followed by some advanced content.",
